body:
kalide's source keeps no symbol the project's call graph proves unreachable, and the dead-code removal is evidence-backed: a candidate is removed only when the call graph reports no incoming `Calls` edge for it AND source inspection finds no non-call use the graph does not model — a function or method taken as a value (assigned to a variable, a struct field, a template func map or an `http.Handler`), an interface method reached only through its interface (`error`, `fmt.Stringer`), a package-level variable or constant initializer, a `//go:embed` target, or a test-only caller. A symbol reached by any of those is live and stays; removal is never inferred from a name or a grep alone.

AC:
- the symbols the call graph reports with no caller, and source inspection reaches through no non-call use — internal/template's `(*Library).Names`, `(*Section).Declarations` and `(*Section).Variants`, and `isSectionHeading` — are removed;
- a call-graph query over non-test `src` symbols with no incoming `Calls` edge returns no symbol that source inspection also reaches through no non-call use;
- the build and the full test suite pass after the removals.
